     "op": "theory",
     "blockId": "p3-reciprocal-relationships-block",
     "replacement": "A **reciprocal relationship** has the form $y=\\frac{k}{x}$, where $k\\ne0$ and $x\\ne0$.\n\nIts graph is not a straight line, so the relationship is **non-linear**.\n\nGraph a reciprocal relationship using these steps:\n\n1. Construct a table of values using the equation.\n2. Graph the table by using the columns as coordinates.\n3. Join the points on each side of $x=0$ to form two separate smooth curves.",
     "autoApply": true,
     "key": "theory|p3-reciprocal-relationships-block",
     "targetFingerprint": "f68b400b2989f6dea144f6d67b82b55a142b50228a847ab0dbb05d7139aea866",
     "applied": true
    }
   ],
   "run": ".booklet-work/pedagogy-audit-v2/s6adv-working-with-functions-6-reciprocal-functions-v1/20261111-090954",
