    {
     "op": "theory",
     "blockId": "p8-theory",
     "replacement": "Another form of a hyperbola is\n\n$$y=\\frac{px+q}{rx+s}$$\n\nwhere $p$, $q$, $r$ and $s$ are constants, $r\\ne0$, $ps-qr\\ne0$ and $x\\ne-\\frac{s}{r}$.\n\nConvert this to standard form by splitting the numerator.",
